    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "\"Hurricane Mitch devastated Central America during the months of October- November of 1998. From 1998 to 2001 the US Geological Survey has been involved along with other federal agencies in the reconstruction effort. This CD consists of a compilation of GIS data layers and computer applications focused on hazard prevention and useful in municipal planning. Each dataset includes layers for a base area of one hundred square kilometers around the urban center of each municipality in the Hurricane Mitch project. The size of the study area and number of database layers may vary depending on data availability. The user may also notice discrepancies between the digital orthophotos the raster and vector layers. These differences are due mostly to differences in scale accuracy and currentness of the data.  Detailed information about the Mitch project and data products can be found at the project's web-site: http://mitchnts1.cr.usgs.gov.\r\n\r\nThe purpose of these datasets is to serve as basic level GIS data in support to hazard prevention for municipalities involved in the Mitch reconstruction efforts and to support the municipalities planning efforts.\"\r\n\r\nNote: Disc J (Puerto Barrios) was unreadable and therefore is not included.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
